; ============================================================================
; x.1sav.label - what a console calls a save, and what it says beneath that
;
; An extension key for the Universal Saves Format, defined by these
; specifications under a name reserved in the Vendor Names registry because the
; value belongs to no single producer.
;
; The root here is the value carried under the key, not a bundle. A bundle
; validates against the format's own schema whatever this holds, since an
; extension value is `any` there; this file is what makes the shape checkable.
; ============================================================================

label = {
    0 => line,     ; title  - what the console lists this save as
  ? 1 => line,     ; detail - what it says about the save beyond its name
}

; Byte length rather than character count, and "" is absence, the way `path`
; has it in the format's own schema. The longest of these on real hardware is a
; PS1 title at 64 bytes, so the ceiling is headroom and not a target.
line = tstr .size (1..256)
